# C# Project Rules

## Project Structure

```
project/
├── MyApp.sln                 # Solution file
├── Directory.Build.props     # Shared MSBuild properties (optional)
├── .editorconfig             # Style and analyzer settings
├── src/
│   └── MyApp/                # Application / library projects
│       └── MyApp.csproj
└── tests/
    ├── unit/                 # Unit tests (in-memory, fast)
    │   └── MyApp.UnitTests/
    └── integration/          # Integration tests
        └── MyApp.IntegrationTests/
```

Use SDK-style `.csproj` files. Enable nullable reference types and implicit usings.

## Tools

| Tool            | Purpose                    |
|-----------------|----------------------------|
| .NET SDK        | Build, restore, run, test  |
| EditorConfig    | Formatting and naming      |
| dotnet format   | Format and analyzer fixes  |
| Roslyn analyzers| Compile-time quality       |
| xUnit           | Testing                    |
| git-cz          | Conventional commits       |

## Conventions

- **Nullable**: `<Nullable>enable</Nullable>` in all projects
- **Namespaces**: Prefer file-scoped namespaces
- **Public APIs**: XML documentation comments on public types and members
- **Primary constructors**: Prefer when they simplify simple types
- **Records**: Prefer for DTOs and value objects
- **Boundaries**: Avoid `dynamic` and untyped `object` at API/domain boundaries

```csharp
// ✅ Good
public sealed record UserId(Guid Value);

public User? GetUser(UserId userId) => ...;

// ❌ Bad
public object GetUser(dynamic userId) => ...;
```

## Formatting and Analyzers

Keep style in `.editorconfig`. After changes:

```bash
dotnet format
dotnet build
```

Never suppress analyzer warnings without a documented justification.

## Commits

**Use git-cz (commitizen)** for conventional commit messages.

```bash
git cz
# Or
cz commit
```

Commit format: `<type>(<scope>): <description>`

| Type     | Usage                        |
|----------|------------------------------|
| feat     | New feature                  |
| fix      | Bug fix                      |
| docs     | Documentation only           |
| refactor | Code change (no fix/feature) |
| test     | Adding/updating tests        |
| chore    | Build, config, dependencies  |

```bash
# ✅ Good
feat(auth): add JWT token refresh endpoint
fix(user): resolve null reference on empty email
test(payment): add integration tests for Stripe

# ❌ Bad
update code
fixed stuff
WIP
```

## Common Commands

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build
dotnet test
dotnet format
dotnet run --project src/MyApp
```
